    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nSherry FitzGerald are delighted to present No. 245 Sutton Park, a superbly extended and renovated family home ideally positioned within this mature and highly sought-after coastal development in the heart of Sutton.\n\nOriginally designed as a four-bedroom, one-bathroom semi-detached residence, the property has been thoughtfully reconfigured and upgraded by its current owners to create a spacious and modern three-bedroom home with two bathrooms, a guest WC, and a stunning open-plan extension to the rear that perfectly caters to contemporary family living.\n\nThe bright and well-appointed accommodation briefly comprises an entrance porch, welcoming hallway, guest WC, comfortable living room, and an impressive extended open-plan kitchen, dining and family room to the rear. This wonderful living space forms the heart of the home, flooded with natural light and opening directly onto a sunny south-west facing rear garden, creating an ideal setting for everyday family life and entertaining alike. To the side, the garage provides valuable storage and offers excellent potential for conversion, subject to the necessary planning permissions, to further enhance the accommodation if desired.\n\nUpstairs, there are three generously proportioned bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with en suite shower room, together with a stylish family bathroom, providing comfortable and practical accommodation for growing families.\n\nThe location is second to none. Sutton Park is a well-established, family-friendly development situated just moments from Sutton Cross and a wealth of local amenities. Residents enjoy easy access to an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools, local shops, supermarkets, cafés, restaurants, church facilities, and a wide range of sporting and recreational amenities. The area is exceptionally well served by public transport, with both Sutton DART Station and numerous bus routes providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and beyond. For outdoor enthusiasts, the property is ideally positioned along the scenic coastal promenade and cycleway, offering breathtaking seaside walks quite literally on the doorstep.\nCombining spacious contemporary accommodation with an outstanding coastal location, No. 245 Sutton Park represents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a turnkey family home in one of North Dublin's most desirable residential settings."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall - 2.45m x 4.88m\nSpacious and bright hallway with glazed windows to either side of hall door, understairs smart storage, guest w.c., semi-solid oak flooring\n\nGuest W.C. - 0.78m x 1.55m\nTiled floor, w.c., wash hand basin and storage press, recessed light\n\nLiving Room - 3.57m x 4.25m\nCarpet, open fireplace, shelving in alcove, double doors to dining\n\nDining - 3.57m x 4.35m\nOpen plan dining into kitchen/family room, semi-solid oak flooring, recessed lights\n\nKitchen/Family Room - 7.54m x 5.51m\nGreat selection of cream gloss floor to ceiling cabinets, integrated full length fridge, separate full length freezer, eye-level dishwasher, cooker, kitchen island, granite countertop with sink, induction hob, cream tiled floor in kitchen and TV point in family room with oak flooring, double doors to south-west facing back garden\n\nUtility Room - 4.06m x 1.63m\nGreat storage including full length wardrobes, location of gas boiler and hot water tank\n\nLanding - 2.60m x 3.85m\nSpacious landing with window to side, hatch to attic with pull down stairs\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.45m x 4.32m\nDouble to rear, walnut effect wardrobes, carpet, door to ensuite\n\nEnsuite - 1.60m x 2.35m\nLarge tiled shower enclosure, shelved storage, w.c, wash hand basin with 2 drawer storage, wall unit, extractor fan, recessed lights, tiled floor, window to rear\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.45m x 4.37m\nDouble to front with light grey built-in wardrobes, carpet\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.47m x 2.40m\nSingle to front, fitted wardrobes, carpet fitted shelving unit\n\nBathroom - 2.52m x 3.26m\nFully tiled, Jacuzzi style bath with shower hose, separate large shower with storage shelf and sliding glass door, w.c, wash hand basin with storage drawers, recessed lights\n\nGarage - 2.45m x 5.24m\nUp and over garage door to front and rear door access into back garden\n\nFront Garden - \nWalled and gated, with off street parking and lawn\n\nBack Garden - \nSouth-west facing back garden, walled, lawn and paved patio and dining area\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Spacious and bright extension</li><li>Garage to side</li><li>Sunny South-West facing rear garden</li><li>Extended open plan kitchen/family room to rear</li><li>Gas boiler (2 years old)</li><li>uPVC Double glazed windows</li><li>Under floor and internal wall insulation</li><li>Replumbed and rewired</li><li>Great space and storage areas in house</li><li>Large attic with pull down ladder</li><li>Off-street parking </li><li>Bayside DART - 4 minute walk approx.</li><li>Shops and services in Bayside/Sutton</li><li>Excellent schools in vicinity</li><li>Great selection of sporting activities in area</ul>"
      },
